+# UX Audit №4 → Actionable Scoping
+
+**Date:** 2026-07-19 · **Branch:** jetbridge · **Source:** fresh-eyes live audit of concourse.home
+(v0.2.195-rc = HEAD `6188b2a8c1`, verified via vcs.revision — the audit saw current code, so every
+finding below survives the latest landings, including `3dadfb55aa` server-derived outcome).
+Report artifact: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/ad17470d-a8b5-4825-8a15-0e841972f850
+
+**Executor legend** — every item is tagged with who can safely do it:
+- `ops` — live-cluster/runbook action, human (or supervised session), minutes not days.
+- `loop` — dispatchable agent ticket (server-side Go only; see Elm rule below). Draft specs at the bottom.
+- `wave` — human Elm session on a branch (like agentic-ui-wave / wave-2). **Elm items are NOT loop
+  tickets** until WF-2 lands: the agent-runner image has no Elm toolchain and no elm-build gate, so an
+  agent could break the bundle and still pass gates. Elm rule: rebuild + commit `web/public/elm.min.js`
+  or the deployed web serves a stale bundle (release-pipeline lesson).
+- `plan` — needs a remainder-style plan (writing-plans discipline) before execution; too big to file raw.
+- `decision` — cheap to build, but the semantics need an owner call first.
+
+**Coordination constraints (from remainders/README + dogfood memory):**
+1. Do not touch the `render.go` refusal chain (contended chokepoint across three in-flight tracks).
+2. Migration numbers: claim the next free slot in remainders/README before any migration; none of the
+   items below require one (L-1 must verify no CHECK constraint exists before adding a status value).
+3. Dispatch timing: push → let the release chain settle → dispatch. Never dispatch while self-upgrade
+   is mid-flight (web restart errors the run and double-spends).
+4. Ticket specs must be self-contained (embed everything; agents get the ticket file + repo checkout).
+
