+## Wave 0 — ops actions (do first; ~45 min total; no code)
+
+### A0-1 · Refresh the agent-runner image  ← kills the chronic P0-2 noise
+The deployed step image is `registry.home/agent-runner:v0.2.167` (web deploy env
+`CONCOURSE_AGENT_STEP_IMAGE`), ~28 versions behind the web. Everything the flight recorder writes
+(`flight/results.json`, `events.ndjson`, `review.json` — agent/runner + cmd/harvest-runner) postdates
+it, so **every** harvest ingests an empty flight volume and `atc/exec/harvest_step.go:598` degrades the
+metrics row to status=error / "flight recorder output missing". This one action turns the runs ledger
+from a wall of fake orange into a real signal, and it is a hard prerequisite for the transcript viewer
+(L-3) and for L-1's semantics to matter.
+
+Runbook:
+1. `fly -t home trigger-job -j jetbridge/build-agent-runner-image -w` → note the tag it pushes
+   (expect `registry.home/agent-runner:v0.2.19x`; job has built only 6 times, it is manual by design).
+2. home-infra bump (ArgoCD self-heals kubectl edits away): clone home-infra with the
+   `concourse-main/github-token` secret, edit `apps/concourse.yaml` → `CONCOURSE_AGENT_STEP_IMAGE` to
+   the new tag, push main, wait ~3 min for sync, confirm with
+   `kubectl -n cicd get deploy concourse-web -o jsonpath=...env`.
+3. Verify cheaply: dispatch a `smoke` workflow ticket (~$0.02–0.12 precedent) and confirm the harvest
+   row records a real summary instead of "flight recorder output missing".
+
+### A0-2 · Queue hygiene (10 min, all via fly/web)
+- Tickets #23/#24 (both Errored, AUP refusal ×2): **abandon** — their T9 scope landed via merged #25;
+  a third respec would spend for nothing. If any T9 remainder is real, refile with reworded vocabulary
+  (see WF-3).
+- Ticket #2 (Queued, no workflow): #12 implements the same fix and is at needs-review. Merge-or-send-back
+  #12 first, then **conclude #2 as superseded** (it never dispatched, so conclude, not abandon).
+- Ticket #1 draft "ticket-core live smoke": served its purpose 2026-07-17 → abandon.
+- Ticket #12 itself is the oldest needs-review (1d 21h): disposition it — that's the audit's own
+  "review latency" finding acting on us.
+- `badpolicy` workflow: give it a description ("negative-test seed: refusal-path validation — do not
+  dispatch") via a v2 import, or accept it as visible cruft; there is no delete verb (see S-6).
