+## Draft ticket specs (Wave 1) — filed as drafts, self-contained
+
+Specs below are what was filed via `fly agent tickets create` (drafts; no workflow pinned; dispatch
+after the next push settles, per constraint 3). Budgets mirror comparable merged tickets.
+
+### L-1 · Recording-incomplete status tier — `$6`
+Files: `agent/schema/metrics.go`, `atc/exec/harvest_step.go`, `atc/exec/agent_step.go`,
+`atc/db/agent_run_metrics_factory.go` (scan path only if needed), `fly/commands/internal/agentrunshelpers` (or
+wherever `fly agent runs` colors outcomes), matching tests.
+Behavior: when flight ingestion finds NO flight artifact / zero flight files (the "never wrote"
+case, as distinct from a read/stream error mid-ingest), the metrics row records `status: "incomplete"`
+with summary `"no flight output (runner image predates flight recorder?)"`. `DeriveOutcome`:
+`incomplete` + succeeded build → `"delivered-unrecorded"` (amber tier, never red); `incomplete` +
+failed/errored build → keep the build verdict. Task 0 must verify no DB CHECK constraint restricts the
+status column (grep migrations for `agent_run_metrics`); if one exists, STOP and report (migration slots
+are coordinated). Wire consumers already degrade gracefully on unknown outcome tokens (`3dadfb55aa`
+fallback chain) — extend fly's known-vocabulary map. Contract guard: `Status` doc comment says
+`ok | failed | error`; update it and the schema tests.
+
+### L-2 · Pipeline-archiver for terminal tickets — `$5`
+New component (pattern: existing reconciler components; wiring in `atc/atccmd/command.go` where K8s
+components wire up, guarded by the dispatcher flag family): every tick, for tickets in
+merged/concluded/abandoned whose `agent-ticket-<id>` pipeline (any instance) is unarchived → archive it
+(existing pipeline archive DB method; team `main`). Never touch draft/queued/dispatched/needs_review/
+errored tickets. Tests with dbfakes; component interval 60s. Explicitly out of scope: deleting
+pipelines, the uninstanced-parent question (W-13 investigates that separately).
+
+### L-3 · Flight-events persistence + read API — `$7`
+At harvest ingestion (`atc/exec/harvest_step.go` ingest path), persist the raw `events.ndjson` bounded
+to the LAST 512 KiB (head-truncation marker line if cut) into the evidence store keyed by
+(ticket, build) — reuse the evidence linkage from #32/#33 (`submitted_by`, sha linkage). New route
+`GET /api/v1/agent/tickets/:ticket_id/runs/:build_id/events` streaming it back
+(`application/x-ndjson`). Route additions follow the #36 six-touchpoint enumeration exactly
+(`atc/routes.go` const + entry, `api_auth_wrappa.go` team-less CheckAgentAuthorizationHandler block +
+tier-pinning specs, handler, scanner/factory read, go-concourse client method, fly plumbing optional).
+Auth tier: same as `GetAgentTicketDiff`/`GetAgentTicketOutcome`. Do NOT touch `render.go`.
+
+### L-4 · Principal kinds — `$3`
+`agent/api` principals list: add `kind: "operator" | "run"` (derive: minted-by-dispatcher run
+principals are `agent-run-<id>` named AND created by the system path — prefer an explicit column-free
+derivation from the existing mint call site over name-prefix sniffing if the mint path can tag it in
+metadata; if only the name is available, prefix-match is acceptable and documented). `fly agent
+principals list` groups operator first, runs collapsed under a count line with `--all` to expand. Web
+consumes in a later wave. Tests both layers.
