+## Sequencing at a glance
+
+1. **A0-1 runner image refresh** (ops, today) → immediately: noise stops on new runs, events data starts landing.
+2. **A0-2 queue hygiene** (ops, today).
+3. **File L-1…L-4 drafts** (done with this doc) → push this branch when convenient → settle → dispatch in
+   the proven cadence (one at a time, judge dispatch-timing).
+4. **Wave 2 "ux4" Elm session** (human, ~a day) → rebuild elm.min.js → push → release chain deploys.
+5. **S-4 in-app diff** pulled forward as the first structural item (smallest, highest trust win).
+6. **S-1 step DAG plan doc** written next (it is the audit's center of gravity), then S-2 transcript viewer.
+7. WF-1a/WF-3 ride along as loop tickets whenever a dispatch slot is free; WF-2 when Elm-loop capacity
+   is wanted.
+
+*Done criteria for the whole scoping: the audit's five P0s each have either a merged fix or an owned
+plan doc; re-running the audit journey (ticket → attempt → step → transcript → review → disposition)
+never leaves the web UI and never shows a contradictory status pair.*
